<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smallholder up on retail buying.</title>
<headline>Tea Smallholder up on retail buying.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd rose 6.25 percent or 2.50 rupees to 42.50 in early Friday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Retail investors are getting into the share, which is cheap and in the favoured plantation sector,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The plantation sector is seen doing well in 1997, due mainly to continuing demand for Sri Lanka tea from the Commonwealth of Independent States, brokers said.</p>
<p>Tea Smallholder processes tea leaf bought from small cultivators.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
